Bleeding time and blood loss seem to respond better to DDAVP in some patients, in whom significant decreases were       
observed, than they do in others. The problem is in identifying those patients in whom a decrease in bleeding time will 
be elicited after administration of DDAVP. Preoperative administration of DDAVP to such patients should significantly   
decrease operative blood loss."}, {"study_index": 23, "title": "The effects of desmopressin acetate (DDAVP) on          
