      {"study_index": 80, "title": "Transjugular liver biopsy ‐ indications, adequacy, quality of specimens, and        
  complications ‐ a systematic review", "abstract": "Transjugular liver biopsy (TJLB) is considered an inferior         
  biopsy, used when percutaneous liver biopsy (PLB) is contraindicated. According to recent literature, specimens with  
