complications. Sixty-four series reporting 7649 TJLBs were evaluated for quality of specimen and safety. Major          
indications were coagulation disorders and/or ascites. Success rate was 96.8%. Fragmentation rate was 34.3%, not        
correlating with length or diagnostic adequacy. With a mean of 2.7 passes, mean CPT number was 6.8. Histological        
diagnosis was achieved in 96.1% of TJLBs, correlating with length (p=0.007) and CPT number (p=0.04). Tru-Cut specimens  
