the proportion of patients who received at least one perioperative allogeneic red cell transfusion. Sixty studies were  
included in the meta-analyses. The largest number of patients (5808) was available for the meta-analysis of aprotinin,  
which significantly decreased exposure to allogeneic blood (odds ratio [OR] 0.31, 95% confidence interval [CI]          
