  revealed that the rate of thrombocytopenia after surgery was higher in the control group (P = 0.012). CONCLUSIONS     
  Our study showed that desmopressin could not reduce the amount of blood loss after CABG. Also, desmopressin did not   
  have a significant effect on coagulation status. Therefore, based on the results of our study, it seems that the use  
  of this medication cannot be a helpful for patients with any indication for CABG."}, {"study_index": 78, "title":     
  "The role of desmopressin in reducing blood loss during lumbar fusions", "abstract": "The effectiveness of            
